		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4521&amp;p=35779#p35779"><![CDATA[
I had this issue on two installs .... one was Win10 install, the the other on Win11.  For both I figured out that the driver wasnt installing due to anti-virus/security settings.   In Windows 10 try turning off security settings -- I cant tell you exactly what I did, I just kept hacking away at it.  In Windows 11 it was tied to Core memory protection settings, try turning that off.   Once I installed the driver from the Baofeng website with security turned off or disabled, the laptops were able to see the radio.  I think the thing that tipped me off was looking at details for the failed install on the Win11 machine.  Windows11 had the driver flagged as incompatible with newer standards and had to be granted access.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8069">KF8DFA</a> — Sun Feb 16, 2025 5:41 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
